# OSRS Ironman Progression Planner — P5-003 review package

P5-003 is the current authorized mode: manual title/category/manual-status creation and optional More details. Active catalog discovery/selection and individual-icon controls are removed. Category artwork controls Graph/Board/editor presentation; saved catalog references, individual overrides and hidden counters remain stored but inactive. Inspector Cancel discards the form and closes; panel hiding preserves drafts. Phase 5 acceptance pending; Phase 6 and text-only dictionary implementation NOT AUTHORIZED.

## Run

Use the existing checkout C:\Users\Jeremiah\OneDrive\Desktop\OSRSLABS\Phase1\osrs-phase1-editor. Run npm run dev and use http://127.0.0.1:4173/ at the existing browser origin for your saved data. No install. Export JSON regularly; source backups do not include browser IndexedDB. Do not run the default build over preserved dist. Exact separate review build, test results, file inventory and Owner walkthrough: HANDOFF.md / TEST_REPORT.md.

## Daily controls

Double-click empty canvas for title, category and manual status; Enter/Create commits, Cancel/Escape creates nothing. More details transfers draft/position to optional notes/grouping inspector. Double-click a goal to quick edit; Board titles and explicit status controls share the same canonical goal. Status never propagates, and only incoming hard prerequisites block readiness. Counters remain hidden and stored.

Category markers agree across Graph (both densities), Board and quick/detailed editors. Changing category updates the displayed symbol; saved individual overrides/references remain inactive. Genuine Combat, Minigame, Quest, Skills and Prayer are locally bundled. Inventory and Achievement Diary are explicit artwork gaps using an original fallback; Custom uses a neutral original diamond. Failed images also use original fallback. No catalog/individual-icon control is active.

Inspector Cancel discards the current unsaved form and closes without a data/history operation; merely toggling the panel preserves drafts. Switching actual targets resolves dirty drafts. Click empty canvas clears selection; dragging pans; Shift-drag selects full visible cards. Actual Shift-click pairing and port dragging create typed connections; Optimize is explicit/undoable and manual dragging remains available. Right-click/Shift+F10 opens contextual actions. Board search/category/readiness/group filters remain available.

Save status and Retry remain visible with panels closed. Import previews require export and explicit replacement confirmation. Failed writes preserve the last committed copy; Retry before reloading unsaved changes. Export preserves inactive references/overrides and exact fractional counters; images are separate assets, not embedded in JSON.

## Content and limits

Owner reports Jagex permission covering third-party artwork sourcing and local bundling for this private planner. Owner-provided, not independently verified; no broader distribution rights implied. Applicable source notices remain retained.

See catalog/CATEGORY_MODE.md and category-artwork-manifest.json for current category coverage, pins and offline preparation. Catalog records, 94 individual-art PNGs, original preparation tooling/provenance/licenses remain in place as inactive/deprecated. Dictionary is deferred. No schema/storage/dependency changes. No complete/current-game content certification, broad redistribution rights, arbitrary-graph routing guarantee or Phase 6 performance/mobile/browser hardening claimed. Historical README preserved at evidence/p5-003-preflight-2026-10-27/README.md-before.
